# Alert display, queueing, pre-emption and coalescing (PS §3, §6.3).

scenario: alert shows, then returns to resting
start media                         -> Compact
alert copied                        -> Alert alert=copied
wait 2999                           -> Alert
wait 1                              -> Compact

scenario: alerts queue and play in order
alert one                           -> Alert alert=one queue=0
alert two                           -> Alert alert=one queue=1
wait 3000                           -> Alert alert=two queue=0
wait 3000                           -> Idle

scenario: higher level pre-empts, and the pre-empted alert replays
alert song active                   -> alert=song
alert meeting timeSensitive         -> alert=meeting queue=1
wait 3000                           -> alert=song
wait 3000                           -> Idle

scenario: coalescing replaces the showing alert and restarts its timer
start media
alert track1 key=track              -> alert=track1
alert other                         -> queue=1
alert track2 key=track              -> alert=track2 queue=1
wait 2000
alert track3 key=track              -> alert=track3
wait 2999                           -> alert=track3

scenario: coalescing replaces a queued alert
alert first
alert track1 key=track              -> queue=1
alert track2 key=track              -> queue=1
wait 3000                           -> alert=track2

scenario: passive never alerts
start battery
alert battery passive               -> Compact queue=0

scenario: full queue drops the oldest lowest-level alert
alert showing critical              -> alert=showing
alert t1 timeSensitive
alert a1
alert a2
alert t2 timeSensitive
alert a3                            -> queue=5
alert a4                            -> queue=5   # a1 dropped
wait 3000                           -> alert=t1
wait 3000                           -> alert=a2
